# PLACEHOLDER art for the wholesome hemp-seed foods — the ones with no THC in them.
#
# Kept in their own file rather than in edibles.mctex on purpose: that file is the dosed set, this
# one is the food-crop set, and the palettes say so. Nothing here has a hemp-green fleck, because
# nothing here is meant to read as psychoactive — these are seed browns and milk creams.
#
# hemp_milk_bucket and siemieniotka are DERIVED: vanilla's milk_bucket and mushroom_stew with only
# the contents retoned, so each reads as the familiar object holding something else. The bucket has
# the same trap the bhang one does — vanilla shares FFFFFF between the milk surface and the specular
# highlight on the metal, so the milk's white needs its own palette character (`A`) or the bucket
# turns cream too.
#
# Note hemp milk is BEIGE, not green. It is pressed from the seed, and seed milk is the colour of
# almond or oat milk; the green drink in this mod is bhang, and they should never be confused at a
# glance in a hotbar.

@palette seeds
# Roasting darkens and reddens the shell. Same three-tone family as the raw seeds, one long
# step down the ramp.
. = none
1 = 1B120A
2 = 4A2C14
3 = 7A4E22

# Toasted seeds are the raw seeds, toasted: this is Warlon Mhite's own item/sativa_seeds.png
# scatter traced pixel for pixel, with two extra seeds tumbled loose so the pan reads as a
# serving rather than a planting. If the seed art is ever redrawn, re-trace this from it.
@texture item/toasted_hemp_seeds 16x16 palette=seeds type=item
................
................
.........12.....
........123.....
....21..13......
...232.....21...
...11......21...
.......31..321..
......211...31..
......31........
..32......23....
..132....321....
...31....11.....
.......21.......
.......321......
................

@palette flapjack
. = none
o = 3A2408
n = 5A3A12
d = 7A5420
m = A87A33
t = C99A4A
s = E8D08A

# A bar, on the archetype vanilla uses for every rectangular slab it draws (item/brick is the
# clearest one): a long, fat, round-ended block lying corner to corner, lit square-on from the
# top left so the tone runs across the short axis -- lit face, midtone, shadow, dark rim. That
# structure is the whole thing; two earlier tries failed because the speckle broke it up and
# because the block was too thin to have a lit face at all. So the seeds are deliberately
# sparse and spaced: `n` for a whole seed standing proud of the pressed mass, `s` for one
# catching the light. Add more and it goes back to reading as a lump.
@texture item/hemp_flapjack 16x16 palette=flapjack type=item
................
................
..........nnn...
........nntttn..
......nntttnmn..
.....nttttmmmmo.
...nntttsmmmmdo.
.nnttttmmmmnddo.
.nttnmmmmddddoo.
.ntmmmmsdddoo...
.nmmmdddddo.....
..odsdddoo......
..odddoo........
...ooo..........
................
................

